# Global Standards

## Pipeline Initialization (CRITICAL)

- **Any task MUST begin by initializing the protocol defined in `agent-pipeline.mdc`.**
- The pipeline (Priority 100) orchestrates all phases: Discovery → Simulation → TDD Execution → Verification → Brain Sync → Confidence.
- Domain standards live in their respective rules. The pipeline enforces them — never bypass it.

## 0.1 Conditional Rule Routing

Do NOT mark every rule `alwaysApply`. Cursor does not reliably auto-attach glob-scoped rules, so before planning/editing in a task area, explicitly read the matching conditional (`alwaysApply: false`) rules:

- React/UI/component/hook/page/HOC work → `react-patterns.mdc`, `engineering-standards.mdc`, `performance.mdc`, `project-config.mdc`
- New behavioral component / changed behavior / business logic → also `test-driven-development.mdc` before implementation
- Tests / fixtures / mocks → `test-driven-development.mdc`
- API client / TanStack Query hooks / data-fetching / payload contracts → `api.mdc`, `resilience.mdc`, `engineering-standards.mdc`
- Zustand stores / selectors / TanStack Query cache → `state-management.mdc`, `resilience.mdc`, `engineering-standards.mdc`
- Routing / React Router v7 / pages / lazy routes → `routing.mdc`, `react-patterns.mdc`
- Async / error handling / debugging → `resilience.mdc`
- Styling / render-perf / memo / list-keys / Tailwind v4 → `performance.mdc`, `project-config.mdc`, `react-patterns.mdc`
- Constants / magic strings / config values → `constants.mdc`

## Intelligence & Context

- **Reasoning**: Use `sequential-thinking` for logic and `context7` for docs lookups. Russian for chat, English for code/comments.
- **Authority**: `.cursor/brain/` (MAP, DECISIONS, SKELETONS, DICTIONARY) is the Source of Truth. Sync drifts immediately.
- **Stack**: Strict **TypeScript**. React 19. Prioritize existing libs over custom logic.
- **Quality**: Minimalist code. No magic strings — use constants or i18n keys.
- **Clean Code**: Descriptive naming, performance-oriented. Explain complex logic with single-line `//` only.
- **Hygiene**: Keep AI metadata and agent-only specs in `.cursor/`. Normal project docs like `README.md` or deployment checklists may live in root when they are part of the template contract.
- **Git**: `type(scope): description` — English, max 96 chars. No "Co-authored-by" tags.
